      "reasons": [
        "The definition’s first sentence (“a group boundary is the social division between groups, including whether movement from one group to another is seen as possible”) is not explicitly supported by the packet text. The packet refers to “group boundary permeability” and examines its effects, but it does not define a “group boundary” as a general “social division” or spell out “movement between groups” as the defining feature.",
        "While the packet does support the later part that impermeable boundaries make the compensation effect more likely (“compensation effect was more likely to emerge when the group boundary was impermeable”), the first sentence contains additional conceptual framing that is not directly supported."
